The hexacolor spire that had pierced heaven and earth, gradually unravelled before their eyes.
The sky that had faded to a dull gray slowly regained its natural color, and before long, as if
having recalled why it was called blue, the azure sky began to clear.
Roswaal: [――――]
With such scenery before him, Roswaal saw tears falling from the eyes of Ezzo beside him.
Whether they were of joy or vexation, it was clear that he had been overcome with emotion.
Although it had taken two people to perform, Roswaal and Ezzo had nevertheless accomplished
a great feat engraved for the first time in the history of magic.
Groupings of four and two colors, the utmost extremity of magical control, formulation of a
technique that did not permit any gaps whatsoever, and the ultimate harmony that could not
have been manifested were there to have been a lag of even an instant―― that, had
surmounted the Divine Dragon’s dragonhalo.
Roswaal’s diligent studies and Ezzo’s research: if either were to have been missing, this magic
would have never been realized.
However――,
Ezzo: [One day, I’ll manage to manifest this technique even by myself…!]
As Ezzo bombasted while shedding ceaseless tears, Roswaal smiled at his side-profile.
Neither was it out of exasperation, nor was it in sarcasm. ――Indeed, that was the very essence
of a magician.
Visualization was important in magic. If it could be visualized, then anything could be
accomplished: that was magic.
Roswaal: [Isn’t that right, Teacher?]
As Roswaal muttered those words, his body began to tip over, and was about to slowly collapse
onto the ground. Ezzo immediately reached out to try to support him, but alas, given how
immensely exhausted he was, he collapsed first.
Then, as the falling Roswaal seemed like he was about to crush Ezzo under him――,
Clind: [――Made it in time. Good news.]
At a precarious juncture, that calm voice and those strong arms successfully saved Roswaal
from falling down, and Ezzo from being squashed.
Having soared through the skies during the battle, Clind had shattered a star before returning to
stand beside them; the versatile steward had at some point put his monocle back on, and
retracted his black horns.
However, his everyday, perfect appearance was flashily dishevelled; it was a form quite unusual,
and unbefitting himself.
Roswaal: [Even so, outside of your butler uniform, you are mostly unharmed, dragonkin truly are
overpooowered~.]
Clind: [Master, if I may be so bold as to correct you. It is not because I am a dragonkin, but
because I, as the dragonkin of the Divine Dragon, am simply special. Assertion.]
Roswaal: […So you really are quite proud after all? It was your receptacle’s fault that we’ve
ended up like this, you know?]
Ezzo: [Don’t point at me when saying that! It is merely that I cannot stand up because my
back… no, because my entire body has gone limp!]
Having fallen face-first, Ezzo was unable to stand up, and yet did not admit defeat. As if to
express sentiments of lament, Clind shrugged his shoulders at that demeanour, but truly, it was
a wonderful quality.
Roswaal: [You’ve changed. You used to be more of a transcendent, detached type.]
Clind: [In that case, I could say the exact same words to you. Return. ――Were you not the one
who was supposed to be clever and underhanded, content to remain a mere mediocre
magician? Confirmation.]
Clind narrowed his eye across his monocle, having perfectly guessed Roswaal’s thinking.
Certainly, he had intended on that. And yet, Roswaal had not done so.
Getting back up after having failed, he had enacted a recklessness he never imagined he ever
would.
That was――,
Roswaal: [It’s simply that I realized something… That all these days, I haaadn’t~ been walking
alone after all.]
Clind & Ezzo: [――――]
At Roswaal’s answer, Clind, and for some reason Ezzo, both fell silent.
Roswaal: [Though perhaps that reason is a bit too obviooous~.]
While only natural for Clind, with whom he had been acquainted a long time, when hyper magic
had been invoked a moment ago, his self had been on the verge of blending together with
Ezzo’s. There, Roswaal had failed to fully conceal his own sentiments and prayers, after all.
Roswaal: [Well, I am quite accustomed to such intermingling of the consciousness, but how did
you manage to remain fine, Ezzo-kun? Normally, you would end up going insaaane~.]
Ezzo: [Don’t speak of such frightening matters so casually! Likely, it is a blessing of the Books of
the Dead. While I was on standby at the Watchtower, I learned the technique to close off my
heart in order to read the Books of the Dead…]
Clind: [I see. This is a magician. Understanding.]
He somewhat felt like Clind had settled on a bit of a rude conclusion, but he would not touch
upon it here.
More importantly, that which they ought to prioritize――,
Clind: [Master, we have certainly fulfilled the duty with which we have been entrusted.
Completion. However…]
Roswaal: [Ah, that’s riiight~.]
As Clind left his words half-finished, Roswaal silently breathed out and looked into the distance.
The same direction as both Clind, and the grounded Ezzo―― he cast his gaze beyond that
horizon.
During the battle against the Divine Dragon, the rocky wasteland that had been completely
terraformed from before, further beyond even that, the final destination of the Aldebaran
Troupe――,
Roswaal: [――The Grand Mogolade Geyser.]
6
At the end of the battle that sundered heaven and earth, when the Divine Dragon had sent its
dragonkin off to go intercept a star, it was confronted with two possible options. ――The
elimination of the magicians, or the fulfillment of its own role.
It would definitely win. Before the surging purple lighting and unleashed great magic, such
arrogance had been lost.
Hence, the Dragon followed the conviction of the personality dwelling within its dragonhusk, and
prioritized the negation of the worst possibility.
――The unleashed breath aimed for a spot far removed from the battlefield, dashing straight
towards it.
Surrounded by a belt of mountains, a colossal hole through the land perforated at their feet――
the Grand Mogolade Geyser.
What could be peered from the ground was merely a pale blue surface of water. But, lurking
underneath, entwined through an intricate system of deep, subterranean veins of water and
magma, was an enormous cavern without peer in this world.
That cavern tunnelled very, very deep, down to the very bottom of the world, leading even
beyond the Great Waterfall. ――To that Grand Mogolade Geyser, the breath was delivered.
???: [――――]
That torrent of white heat was swallowed by the geyser’s mouth, a thunderous cacophony
quaking the bedrock. That instant, the water’s surface, having appeared exceedingly still, began
to rumble―― and erupted.
That phenomenon was neither an explosion that fissured the land, nor was it an eruption that
spouted fire.
Roaring as if heaven and earth had been inverted, a silver column of water towered up from the
geyser’s mouth, far higher than the scale of a few hundred meters, it surpassed even the peaks
of the surrounding mountain range as it pierced the heavens. The water pillar basked in the rays
of the sun, shimmering in seven colors; while scattering vapour and clangour, it rained a
tremendous amount of water droplets down onto the ground.
――When that fountain ceased, a brand new cavern would be bored into the land.
That was a great cavern of a scale inconceivable on the surface, and when the mouth of that
abyss opened up beyond the light and vapour, awaiting beyond would be a sky differing to the
one present above.
The final roar of the Divine Dragon served as a surefire awakening, rousing the Grand
Mogolade Geyser from its slumber.
――The Following Star’s journey to put an end to Natsuki Subaru, was nigh on its coda.
《Fin》
